,"gene_symbol":"RNF4","gene_symbol_current":"RNF4","gene_id":"ENSG00000063978","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":1.58583e-33,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.124748,"nucleus_score":-12.1855,"pct_ad":0.417899,"pct_control":0.445638,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.751245,"donor_log2fc":-0.0514864,"donor_lfcse":0.0381027,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.0156476},{"cell_type":"Mic","gene_symbol":"RNF4","gene_symbol_current":"RNF4","gene_id":"ENSG00000063978","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.093146,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.0834122,"nucleus_score":-1.92973,"pct_ad":0.262396,"pct_control":0.275806,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.874834,"donor_log2fc":-0.0431494,"donor_lfcse":0.0674599,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.0143574},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_symbol":"RNF4","gene_symbol_current":"RNF4","gene_id":"ENSG00000063978","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.792244,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.0148473,"nucleus_score":-0.41553,"pct_ad":0.231733,"pct_control":0.234039,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":-0.0386087,"donor_lfcse":0.0678277,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-8.69924e-06},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"RNF4","gene_symbol_current":"RNF4","gene_id":"ENSG00000063978","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.00797834,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.0681794,"nucleus_score":-2.79009,"pct_ad":0.172997,"pct_control":0.181185,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.868586,"donor_log2fc":-0.0436647,"donor_lfcse":0.0484389,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.0179416}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000063978","entrez_id":["6047"],"uniprot":["P78317"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene contains a RING finger motif and acts as a transcription regulator. This protein has been shown to interact with, and inhibit the activity of, TRPS1, a transcription suppressor of GATA-mediated transcription. Transcription repressor ZNF278/PATZ is found to interact with this protein, and thus reduce the enhancement of androgen receptor-dependent transcription mediated by this protein. Studies of the mouse and rat counterparts suggested a role of this protein in spermatogenesis. A pseudogene of this gene is found on chromosome 1.[provided by RefSeq, Jul 2010].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P78317","text":"E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase which binds polysumoylated chains covalently attached to proteins and mediates 'Lys-6'-, 'Lys-11'-, 'Lys-48'- and 'Lys-63'-linked polyubiquitination of those substrates and their subsequent targeting to the proteasome for degradation (PubMed:18408734, PubMed:19307308, PubMed:35013556). Regulates the degradation of several proteins including PML and the transcriptional activator PEA3 (PubMed:18408734, PubMed:19307308, PubMed:20943951). Involved in chromosome alignment and spindle assembly, it regulates the kinetochore CENPH-CENPI-CENPK complex by targeting polysumoylated CENPI to proteasomal degradation (PubMed:20212317). Regulates the cellular responses to hypoxia and heat shock through degradation of respectively EPAS1 and PARP1 (PubMed:19779455, PubMed:20026589). Alternatively, it may also bind DNA/nucleosomes and have a more direct role in the regulation of transcription for instance enhancing basal transcription and steroid receptor-mediated transcriptional activation (PubMed:12885770). Catalyzes ubiquitination of sumoylated PARP1 in response to PARP1 trapping to chromatin, leading to PARP1 removal from chromatin by VCP/p97 (PubMed:35013556)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}